### Orientation Prompt

"I want to back up the app's data to the user's own Google
Drive — no central server, the user owns their data. I don't
want backup files cluttering their normal Drive though.
Research the right Google Drive approach for app backups
and explain it before we build."

### Google Cloud Setup

"Walk me through setting up Google Drive access for a
client-side web app, step by step:
- creating the Google Cloud project
- enabling the Drive API
- configuring the OAuth consent screen
- creating an OAuth client ID for our GitHub Pages URL
- scoping it to ONLY appDataFolder — minimum permission,
  nothing else

Tell me exactly what to enter at each screen. We want the
narrowest possible scope — we can only touch our own
backup folder, never the user's real files."

### Build Step 2 — The Google Auth Service

"Read CLAUDE.md and our auth.service.ts so you follow our
patterns. Build a GoogleDriveService that handles sign-in
with Google using the OAuth client we just set up.

Expose it as signals like the rest of the app — whether
the user is signed in, their account info, and any auth
error. Use inject(). Follow our AuthService patterns where
they fit."

### Build Step 3 — Backup

"Add a backup method to GoogleDriveService. It should take
our app data — all expenses and budgets from the ExpenseStore —
serialize it to JSON, and write it to the appDataFolder as a
single backup file. If a backup already exists, update it
rather than creating duplicates.

Add a 'Back up now' button to a setting screen which should
be accessible from the main window using a settings icon,
with a loading
state and a success confirmation showing the backup time.
Read expense.store.ts so you pull the data correctly."

### Build Step 4 — Restore

"Add a restore method. It reads the backup file from
appDataFolder, parses it, and loads the expenses and budgets
back into the ExpenseStore.

Because restore OVERWRITES current data, show a confirmation
first — 'This will replace your current data with the backup
from [date]. Continue?' Add a 'Restore from backup' button
with that confirmation."

### The Retrospective

"Update CLAUDE.md: the Google Drive integration — the OAuth
setup, the appDataFolder approach, the GoogleDriveService and
its signals, and the backup/restore methods. Note the scope
is appDataFolder-only by design. Also note this stays
client-side — no server was added."
